  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 155 AM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nOur weather pattern becomes much more active Friday and beyond as \nthe ridge finally breaks down. Southwesterly flow aloft will \nincrease Friday, especially across the western half of our region. \nIncreasing lift and moisture will lead to the development of showers \nand thunderstorms along and west of the Pecos River. As convection \nspreads east overnight Friday into Saturday, it will be met with \nplenty of resistance as the upper dynamics fade. As troughing \nremains to our west much of the weekend, several disturbances will \ncross the region withing southwesterly flow aloft. Expect multiple \nrounds of rain, especially over the higher terrain and SE NM where \nflash flooding will be possible. \n\nTemperatures will remain above normal until this weekend when clouds \nand showers arrive. Models show a cold front arriving early next \nweek, but differ on the strength.",
